From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:43:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Load i2c_mux_pca954x before nvsw_sn2201 on SN2201

nvsw_sn2201 creates the main pca9548 mux at 1-0070 from its i2c_mlxcpld
completion callback and immediately calls i2c_get_adapter() for the mux
channel buses. i2c_mux_pca954x is a module that is only loaded on demand
by udev, so on SN2201 the platform driver usually wins the race, logs
"Failed to get adapter for bus 2" and destroys the mux. Every board bus
(i2c-2 .. i2c-13) is then missing, leaving hw-management without the
system EEPROM, PSU, fan and CPLD devices.

Add a softdep so modprobe loads i2c_mux_pca954x before nvsw_sn2201.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
---
 usr/etc/modprobe.d/hw-management.conf | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/etc/modprobe.d/hw-management.conf b/usr/etc/modprobe.d/hw-management.conf
index 636be61e..e80cf357 100644
--- a/usr/etc/modprobe.d/hw-management.conf
+++ b/usr/etc/modprobe.d/hw-management.conf
@@ -21,3 +21,8 @@ blacklist amd_sfh
 blacklist amd_pmf
 install amd_sfh /bin/true
 install amd_pmf /bin/true
+# nvsw_sn2201 instantiates the main pca9548 mux and immediately looks up its
+# channel buses; make sure the mux driver is loaded first so it binds
+# synchronously. Otherwise the platform driver races udev, fails with
+# "Failed to get adapter for bus 2" and tears the mux down.
+softdep nvsw_sn2201 pre: i2c_mux_pca954x
